From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:31:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tcg: taint shadow pass hooks

The engine side of the taint capability (exec/taint.h, accel/tcg/taint.c
in the overlay). With ANALYSIS_CAP_TAINT provisioned:

- translator_loop runs taint_gen_tb() on a TB whose cflags carry the new
  CF_TAINT bit, after plugin injection and before optimization; a second
  new bit, CF_TAINT_CHECK, marks the check-only variant of elastic taint
  (the pass leaves a TB through cpu_loop_exit or TB_EXIT_REQUESTED
  whenever it switches variant, so the two never chain and cpu_exec needs
  no check of its own);
- tcg_exec_realizefn creates the shadow globals once the target's TCG
  globals exist (taint_tcg_init) and allocates each vCPU's shadow CPU
  state and shadow TLB (taint_vcpu_init, CPUState::taint_senv);
- cputlb flushes the shadow TLB wherever it flushes or refills a TLB
  entry, and exports tlb_peek_ram_addr(), a no-fill, no-fault lookup of
  the ram_addr behind a mapped address for the shadow slow path;
- invalidate_and_set_dirty(), which every device, DMA and loader write into
  RAM reaches and no CPU store does, clears the written bytes' shadow;
- helpers that write guest memory from C report each write
  (taint_helper_copy/_fill) so the shadow moves with the data: target/arm's
  FEAT_MOPS steps (CPY*, SET*; glibc's memcpy/memset on a CPU that has
  them) and DC ZVA, and RISC-V cbo.zero;
- target/arm registers get_user_reg/set_user_reg (now one user_reg_ptr())
  as helpers whose CPU-state field the mode picks at run time, so the
  shadow follows a 32-bit kernel's return to user (LDM ^ loads r0-r14
  through set_user_reg); its register bank switches done in C (the
  stack pointers on AArch64 exception entry and return, AArch32's
  switch_mode) copy the shadow too (taint_env_copy);
- target/mips's partial-word stores (swl, swr, sdl, sdr) store a register
  a byte at a time in C: they report each byte and which byte of the value
  it was (taint_helper_store_lane), and the pass stages the value's shadow
  before the call; ll and lld load in C, and the pass reads the result's
  shadow from RAM after the call as for a qemu_ld;
- liveness_pass_2 creates a direct temporary only for the indirect
  globals a TB uses, not for every one: the shadow globals are indirect
  (based on taint_senv), and on MIPS64 one per guest global left too few
  of TCG_MAX_TEMPS for a single instruction (an assertion in tb_gen_code).
  Without taint no built target has indirect globals, so this pass does
  not run there;
- -analysis-capabilities accepts "taint", and configure_accelerators
  refuses it without TCG (as it refuses -icount).

Every hook is behind taint_active (false unless taint is enabled in a
replay) or the capability, so an engine without taint pays one predicted
branch on TLB fills and flushes, device writes and those helpers, and
nothing in cpu_exec or in translated code.

